ONLINE BANKING SYSTEM IN C PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE
ICT113 Mini Project Report
1.0 Introduction

This project presents a simple Online Banking System developed using the C programming language. The system simulates basic banking operations such as account registration, login authentication, balance inquiry, deposits, withdrawals, fund transfer, and password change.

The project is designed as a file-based system, where each user account is stored in a separate binary file using the user’s phone number as the filename. This approach allows persistent data storage without the use of external database systems.

The implementation is inspired by a tutorial-based learning approach and was developed to strengthen understanding of core C programming concepts such as structures, file handling, loops, conditional statements, and string manipulation.

2.0 Objectives of the Project

The main objectives of this project are:

To apply fundamental C programming concepts in a real-world simulation.
To implement user authentication using file handling techniques.
To simulate basic banking operations using structured programming.
To understand data storage using binary files in C.
To improve problem-solving skills through system design and logic building.

